<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi chosen to lead India</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress parliamentary party elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> as its leader after the sudden death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lal-bahadur-shastri">Lal Bahadur Shastri</a>. Sworn in five days later, she became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first and only woman prime minister.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-4">4 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon says the Beatles are 'more popular than Jesus'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The remark appeared in an interview in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>'s Evening Standard and passed unnoticed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Reprinted in the US months later, it led to record burnings and radio bans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-13">13 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court decides Miranda v. Arizona</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Court ruled that suspects must be told of their right to remain silent and to have a lawyer before police questioning. The 'Miranda warning' became standard practice.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-29">29 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Beatles play their last concert for paying fans</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-beatles">The Beatles</a> played a half-hour set at Candlestick Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>. They then gave up touring to concentrate on studio albums such as Sgt. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">Pepper</a>'s Lonely Hearts Club Band.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">Pepper</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-6">6 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hendrik Verwoerd is stabbed to death in parliament</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s prime minister, chief architect of apartheid, was killed in the House of Assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a> by parliamentary messenger Dimitri Tsafendas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apartheid">Apartheid</a> continued under his successors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-21">21 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">A colliery spoil tip engulfs a school at Aberfan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> waste tip slid down onto the Welsh village of Aberfan, burying Pantglas Junior School. The disaster killed 144 people, 116 of them children, and an inquiry blamed the National Coal Board.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent-declaration" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tashkent-declaration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tashkent-declaration">Tashkent Declaration</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tashkent Declaration was the peace agreement signed on 10 January 1966 by Prime Minister Lal Bahadur Shastri of India and President Ayub Khan of Pakistan at Tashkent, with Soviet mediation by Alexei Kosygin.</p></div></li></ol></section>
